// A first song: the opening of ふるさと (Furusato, 1914; words Takano Tatsuyuki, music Okano
// Teiichi; in the public domain). The part names its words, `lyrics` holds them, the score's
// row prints them, and the `singer` line is what makes them heard. Open the preview and press Play.
octave relative
time 3/4
key g major
tempo 80
part melody { instrument alto  lyrics words }
section A {
  melody {
    g'4 g g | a4. b8 a4 | b4 b c | d2. |
  }
  lyrics words {
    う さ ぎ | お い し | か の や | ま |
  }
}
form { A }
singer female on melody
score { staff melody  lyrics words }
